    "body_rule": "Profile section 3. A REQUEST has a body when it carries Content-Length above zero, any Transfer-Encoding, or a Content-Length that is not a plain decimal, or when a non-empty body arrives whatever the headers said. A RESPONSE has a body when it has content; its Content-Length is not evidence, since a HEAD or 304 response announces a length it does not send. A body obliges a covered content-digest, and a response to a request that had a body must also cover \"content-digest\";req.",
    "freshness": "Profile section 6: refuse created < now - max_age - skew or created > now + skew as signature-stale, then expires < now - skew as signature-expired. Each case gives the now it assumes, in seconds since the epoch.",
    "case_policy": "A case may carry a policy object whose fields extend this one: expected_keyid, the AID a client expects a response from (profile R1); authorities, the @authority values a verifier serves (profile section 3)."
